LeetCode 1907 — Count Salary Categories (Medium):

Table: Accounts
+-------------+------+
| Column Name | Type |
+-------------+------+
| account_id  | int  |
| income      | int  |
+-------------+------+
account_id is the primary key for this table. Each row contains information about the monthly income for one bank account. AlgoMonster

Task
Write an SQL query to report the number of bank accounts of each salary category. The salary categories are: AlgoMonster

"Low Salary": All the salaries strictly less than $20000. AlgoMonster
"Average Salary": All the salaries in the inclusive range [$20000, $50000]. AlgoMonster
"High Salary": All the salaries strictly greater than $50000. AlgoMonster

The result table must contain all three categories. If there are no accounts in a category, then report 0. Return the result table in any order. AlgoMonster
The query result format is in the following example.

Example
Input — Accounts table:
+------------+--------+
| account_id | income |
+------------+--------+
| 3          | 108939 |
| 2          | 12747  |
| 8          | 87709  |
| 6          | 91796  |
+------------+--------+
Output:
+----------------+----------------+
| category       | accounts_count |
+----------------+----------------+
| Low Salary     | 1              |
| Average Salary | 0              |
| High Salary    | 3              |
+----------------+----------------+

Solution 1
----------
WITH salary_categories AS (
    SELECT
        account_id,
        CASE
            WHEN income < 20000 THEN 'Low Salary'
            WHEN income >= 20000 AND income <= 50000 THEN 'Average Salary'
            ELSE 'High Salary'
        END as category
    FROM accounts
)
, categories AS (
    SELECT 'Low Salary' as category
    UNION 
    SELECT 'Average Salary' as category
    UNION
    SELECT 'High Salary' as category
)

SELECT
    c.category,
    IFNULL(COUNT(account_id), 0) AS accounts_count
FROM categories c
LEFT JOIN salary_categories sc ON c.category = sc.category
GROUP BY c.category;

Solution 2
-----------
SELECT 'Low Salary' as category, COUNT(*) as accounts_count FROM accounts WHERE income < 20000
UNION
SELECT 'Average Salary' as category, COUNT(*) as accounts_count FROM accounts WHERE income >= 20000 AND income <= 50000
UNION
SELECT 'High Salary' as category, COUNT(*) as accounts_count FROM accounts WHERE income > 50000;
